ot v4.8.dev (00932449c) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8266) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-10105 CPU @ 3.70GHz (8 threads) - 15.89 GiB memory - WASAPI (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe command palette is meant to reorder so the most recently used commands are on top.  As per:\n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/51800\n\nHowever, when we execute a command and open the Command Palette again, without typing on the search at all, the order is not updated. Instead it updates when we search.\n\n<img width=\"602\" height=\"472\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89a7b363-42a9-4bdd-82ff-6c16789e5954\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open the command palette.\n- Execute a command that is not the top one, without typing on the search.\n- Open the command palette.\n- Notice the command you executed is not on the top, the order has not changed.\n\nNote: To get the list to update the order type anything and erase it.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNA","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":